    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0558" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/7: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Biddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-01">September 1,
                        1939</date>.<lb/>[Received September 1—5:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. Department’s 52, September l.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d573-f1"/> My 245,
                    September 1. For the President and Secretary.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>With further reference to President’s message Beck imparted (but not for
                        publication) that strict instructions described my previous cable had been
                        issued with initial mobilization orders. Moreover consistent with Polish
                        restraint not one Polish plane had crossed over German territory during
                        today’s fighting.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Beck was concerned and was investigating reports that 70 civilians were
                        killed in Lwów and considerable damage done in Gdynia as result of
                        unprovoked air attacks.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
